{"name":"Brown Thrush","hex":"#906151","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"brown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour like that of chocolate or coffee.","One of the colour balls used in snooker, with a value of 4 points."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a brown color/colour.","Gloomy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brown"},{"term":"thrush","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of numerous species of songbirds of the cosmopolitan family Turdidae, such as the song thrush, mistle thrush, bluebird, and American robin.","A female singer."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fungal infection caused by species of genus Candida, affecting the mouth or vagina; candidiasis."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thrush"}],"entries":[{"title":"Brown-headed thrush","blocks":[{"text":"The brown-headed thrush, sometimes known as the brown thrush, is a species of bird in the family Turdidae. It breeds in Sakhalin, the Kuril Islands and Japan; it winters in south toward the Ryukyu Islands, Taiwan, Hainan and the northern Philippines. Its natural habitat is temperate forests."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Akahara_08f2218.jpg/330px-Akahara_08f2218.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brown-headed_thrush"},{"title":"Brown thrasher","blocks":[{"text":"The brown thrasher, sometimes erroneously called the brown thrush or fox-coloured thrush, is a bird in the family Mimidae, which also includes the New World catbirds and mockingbirds. The brown thrasher is abundant throughout the eastern and central United States and southern and central Canada, and it is the only thrasher to live primarily east of the Rockies and central Texas. It is the state bird of Georgia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Brown_thrasher_in_CP_%2802147%29.jpg/330px-Brown_thrasher_in_CP_%2802147%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brown_thrasher"},{"title":"Thrush (bird)","blocks":[{"text":"The thrushes are a passerine bird family, Turdidae, with a worldwide distribution. The family was once much larger before biologists reclassified the former subfamily Saxicolinae, which includes the chats and European robins, as Old World flycatchers. Thrushes are small to medium-sized ground living birds that feed on insects, other invertebrates, and fruit. Some unrelated species around the world have been named after thrushes due to their similarity to birds in this family."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Psophocichla_litsitsirupa_%28Etosha%29.jpg/330px-Psophocichla_litsitsirupa_%28Etosha%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thrush_(bird)"},{"title":"Brown","blocks":[{"text":"Brown is a color. It can be thought as a darker, typically desaturated shade of orange, and can often be produced by combining red and yellow with another color, namely blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg/330px-Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brown"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Toxostoma_rufum_-Virginia%2C_USA_-adult_and_juvenile-8.jpg/500px-Toxostoma_rufum_-Virginia%2C_USA_-adult_and_juvenile-8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Toxostoma_rufum_-Virginia%2C_USA_-adult_and_juvenile-8.jpg/500px-Toxostoma_rufum_-Virginia%2C_USA_-adult_and_juvenile-8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Adult with juvenile (r) in Virgini